    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d487">

                <pb facs="0669" n="561" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg561"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote to Mr. Wharton</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-06-06"><hi rendition="#italic">June 6,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Immediately on receipt of your note of the
                    4th instant relative to the proposed <hi rendition="#italic">modus vivendi</hi>
                    in Behring Sea, I communicated its contents to the Marquis of Salisbury by
                    telegraph. I have now the honor to inform you that late last night I received a
                    telegraphic reply from his lordship, of which the substance is contained in the
                    inclosed memorandum.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian.
                    Pauncefote</hi>.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d487-a1.xml" xpointer="d487-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
